# Recognition is a byte-exact, evidence-producing repo: hashes, signatures, packet
# manifests, sha256sums, attestation bundles, and the hash-chained receipts are all
# verified over EXACT file bytes. Any line-ending conversion (e.g. Windows CI checking
# files out as CRLF) would change those bytes and break signature/packet verification.
#
# Therefore: NEVER convert line endings for any file, on any platform.
* -text
